# Walkthrough: Displaying Last Price & Last Close Price When Market is Closed

## Overview
We have resolved the user request to fix the platform so that when the market is closed (and during regular operation), all instruments display both their **Last Price (LTP)** and their **Last Close Price (Previous Close)**, alongside net change and change percentage.

---

## Changes Made

### 1. Backend & Broker Updates
- [backend/src/brokers/IBrokerAdapter.ts](file:///d:/python-pron/paper-trading-platform/backend/src/brokers/IBrokerAdapter.ts):
  - Added optional `closePrice?: number;` to [`QuoteDTO`](file:///d:/python-pron/paper-trading-platform/backend/src/brokers/IBrokerAdapter.ts#L46-L70).
- [backend/src/brokers/zerodha/ZerodhaAdapter.ts](file:///d:/python-pron/paper-trading-platform/backend/src/brokers/zerodha/ZerodhaAdapter.ts):
  - Enriched both live [`KiteConnect.getQuote`](file:///d:/python-pron/paper-trading-platform/backend/src/brokers/zerodha/ZerodhaAdapter.ts#L124) and fallback quote generation to include `closePrice` and `close`.
- [backend/src/websocket/priceFeedGateway.ts](file:///d:/python-pron/paper-trading-platform/backend/src/websocket/priceFeedGateway.ts):
  - Ensured all WebSocket ticks emitted via `tick` event include `lastPrice`, `closePrice`, `close`, `netChange`, and `changePercent`.
  - Maintained zero price jitter when market is closed (`isMarketOpen()` is false).
- [backend/src/routes/market.routes.ts](file:///d:/python-pron/paper-trading-platform/backend/src/routes/market.routes.ts):
  - Enriched every returned instrument in [`GET /api/market/instruments`](file:///d:/python-pron/paper-trading-platform/backend/src/routes/market.routes.ts#L56) with `lastPrice`, `closePrice`, `close`, `netChange`, and `changePercent`.

### 2. Frontend Updates
- [frontend/src/services/api.ts](file:///d:/python-pron/paper-trading-platform/frontend/src/services/api.ts):
  - Added `closePrice?: number; close?: number; netChange?: number; changePercent?: number;` to the [`Instrument`](file:///d:/python-pron/paper-trading-platform/frontend/src/services/api.ts#L18-L27) interface.
- [frontend/src/pages/Trade.tsx](file:///d:/python-pron/paper-trading-platform/frontend/src/pages/Trade.tsx):
  - **Top Index Ticker Bar (`TickerBar`)**:
    - Displayed for each index (`NIFTY 50`, `BANKNIFTY`, `FINNIFTY`, `INDIA VIX`, `MIDCAP`):
      - Symbol label
      - **LTP**: `₹23,724.67`
      - **Change**: `+23.72 (+0.10%)`
      - **Close Badge**: `Close: ₹23,700.95`
  - **Watchlist Symbol Cards**:
    - Fixed `wPrices[r.instrumentToken]` object unpack bug so prices never display as `"—"`.
    - Right side of each card now displays:
      - **LTP (Last Price)** in high-contrast bold font (green if $\ge$ close, red if $<$ close).
      - **Net Change & %** (e.g. `+23.72 (+0.10%)`).
      - **Close Price** badge (e.g. `Close: ₹23,700.95`).
    - Expanded accordion drawer displays an instrument price summary pill:
      - `Last: ₹...  |  Last Close: ₹...  |  Chg: +... (+...%)`
  - **Chart Toolbar Header Chip (`t-sym-chip`)**:
    - Displays selected symbol's `LTP`, `Chg & %`, and a `Last Close: ₹...` pill.
  - **Order Ticket Panel**:
    - Displays an order ticket summary card with `Last Price (LTP)`, `Last Close Price`, and `Market Open / Closed` indicator.
  - **Market Depth & Option Chain Modals**:
    - Shows both `Spot LTP` and `Last Close` prices.
  - **Positions & Holdings**:
    - Corrected `wPrices` lookup with `.ltp` and displayed both `LTP` and `Close`.

